This licence covers this repository's own source code and documentation:
the three modules' ColdFire sources, their manifests and their READMEs. It
does not extend to any Elektron Music Machines firmware, which is not
distributed here and remains the property of its copyright holder; every
image is built by the user from their own copy of the official OS with
octabam (https://github.com/sambanks/octabam, MIT, Sam Banks), whose build
system these manifests are written for. The displaced stock instructions a
hook site replays (a few bytes per site) are carried the way every octabam
ColdFire module carries them. Nothing in this project is endorsed by,
supported by or affiliated with Elektron. Octatrack and Elektron are
trademarks of Elektron Music Machines MAV AB, used only to identify the
hardware this project targets.

---

This module's files under upstream/ are the author's own, pinned to
https://github.com/timhastie/octatrick-modules at
39dc5d8ca285c14674b66a452f58a5a0364efb96 (tag v2.14): upstream/sy-drum/ is
that repository's sy-drum/ byte for byte except manifest.py, whose stock
expectations are written as stock_guard(address, length, sha256) here
(sdk/imports/sy-drum-39dc5d8.json lists every file and its hash), and
upstream/synth/engine_abi.inc is its synth/engine_abi.inc. The author's
LICENSE is retained unchanged as upstream/LICENSE.

The Modwerk packaging in this folder (manifest.py, octamod.module.json,
README.md, TESTING.md, verify.py, stock-guards.json, media/LICENSE.md and the
thumbnail in presentation/) is by Tim Hastie under the MIT licence above. The
LCD captures in media/ are declared separately in media/LICENSE.md.

SY DRUM is modelled on the 1979 Pearl Syncussion SY-1, written from a study of
that unit's circuit. It is not affiliated with or endorsed by Pearl or
Behringer. Syncussion is a trademark of its owner.
